import "../../../../sass/accessibility.scss";
import { urls } from "../../../../data";

<div class="a11y-pattern-content">
  <h1>Action Menu Accessibility</h1>
  <h2>Best Practices</h2>
  <p>
    An action menu is an ARIA menu. The <code>action-menu</code> element
    <strong>must</strong> have <code>role="menu"</code> and an accessible name:
    when the menu opens from a trigger, use <code>aria-labelledby</code>
    pointing at the trigger; otherwise use <code>aria-label</code> .
  </p>
  <p>
    Each command <strong>must</strong> have a role of <code>menuitem</code> ,
    <code>menuitemcheckbox</code> or <code>menuitemradio</code> . A checkable
    command <strong>must</strong> set <code>aria-checked</code> to
    <code>"true"</code> or <code>"false"</code> . The tick icon is decorative
    and <strong>must</strong> be hidden with <code>aria-hidden="true"</code> ;
    screen readers get the checked state from <code>aria-checked</code> .
  </p>
  <p>
    Use an action menu only for commands that run on the current page. For
    choices that narrow a set of results, use a
    <a href=`${urls.components}/filter-menu`>filter menu</a> ; for links, use a
    <a href=`${urls.components}/navigation-menu`>navigation menu</a> . Do not
    mix commands and links in one menu.
  </p>
  <h2>Interaction Design</h2>
  <p>
    This section provides interaction design for keyboard and screen reader
    users.
  </p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <p>
    Focus moves to the first enabled command when the menu opens. The
    <code>UP ARROW</code> and <code>DOWN ARROW</code> keys move focus between
    commands, and <code>HOME</code> and <code>END</code> move to the first and
    last. Typing a character moves focus to the next command that starts with
    it. <code>ENTER</code> or <code>SPACEBAR</code> runs the focused command,
    toggles a checkbox action, or selects a radio action.
  </p>
  <p>
    When an action menu opens from a trigger, running an enabled command closes
    it, including a checkbox or radio action. <code>ESCAPE</code> closes the
    menu and returns focus to the trigger. Moving focus or clicking outside
    closes it without moving focus.
  </p>
  <h3>Screen Reader</h3>
  <p>
    A command <strong>must</strong> announce as a menu item. A checkbox action
    announces as a menu item checkbox and a radio action as a menu item radio,
    each with its checked or not checked state. A disabled command sets
    <code>aria-disabled="true"</code> and announces as dimmed or unavailable.
  </p>
</div>
